1 SYSTEM_VOLUME
    Each time govax starts, it:

    1.  Mounts the system volume on DUA0: (below), making it the first
        time.
    2.  Mounts the containers the --mount and --mount-write options name,
        and the default volume (vax.default.volume.file), on DUA1: unless
        configured otherwise.
    3.  Runs SYS$MANAGER:STARTUP.COM from the system volume, at command
        level 1, as a login command procedure.  It defines the system
        logical names, sizes the memory (INITIALIZE/VAX and VMINIT, from
        the vax.memory.* settings), loads SYS$SYSTEM:DEFAULT.ROM,
        assembles SYS$SOURCES:KERNEL.ASM and starts it, defines TTA0: and
        NLA0:, and last runs SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM.
    4.  Installs the page file, with paging on.
    5.  Runs vax.startup.procedure, if that names a procedure.
    6.  Runs the command on govax's command line and exits, or else
        shows the VAX> prompt.

    The system volume is an ODS-2 container, by default
    ~/.govax/govax-system.dsk, labeled GOVAXSYS, holding govax's own
    files:

        [SYSTEM.SYSEXE]  SYS$SYSTEM     DEFAULT.ROM, PAGEFILE.SYS
        [SYSTEM.SYSMGR]  SYS$MANAGER    STARTUP.COM, SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM,
                                        CONSOLE.DCL, DEBUG.DCL
        [SYSTEM.SYSHLP]  SYS$HELP       CONSOLE.HLP, DEBUG.HLP
        [SYSTEM.SYSLIB]  SYS$LIBRARY,   STARLET.MLB, FORSYSDEF.TLB,
                         SYS$SHARE      FTNRTL.EXE
        [SYSTEM.SOURCES] SYS$SOURCES    KERNEL.ASM, SSDEF.ASM, FTNRTL's
                                        sources, STARLET.MAR and
                                        STARLETDEF.MAR, BUILDFTN.COM,
                                        BUILDSTARLET.COM
        [SYSTEM]         SYS$SYSROOT    GOVAX$FILES.DAT, the list of
                                        files govax supplied

    govax defines SYS$SYSDEVICE and SYS$SYSROOT when it mounts the
    volume; STARTUP.COM defines the rest, so you can see and change them.
    MACRO, FORTRAN, LINK, and RUN find their libraries and FTNRTL.EXE
    through SYS$LIBRARY and SYS$SHARE ahead of the copies built into
    govax, so an edited kernel, a rebuilt FTNRTL, or a rebuilt macro
    library is the one used.

    Your own startup commands belong in SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM:
    govax makes it once and never changes it.  Every other file is
    govax's: when a newer govax has a new copy of a file you haven't
    changed, it writes its copy as a new version (the old one stays); a
    file you have changed is kept, and %MOUNT-I-SYSKEPT says so once for
    each new copy.

    To rebuild FTNRTL.EXE or STARLET.MLB from the sources, as new versions
    in SYS$SHARE and SYS$LIBRARY:

        VAX> @SYS$SOURCES:BUILDFTN
        VAX> @SYS$SOURCES:BUILDSTARLET

    Delete the versions you made to go back to govax's.

    Only one govax session at a time can write the volume; a second
    mounts it read-only (%MOUNT-I-SYSREADONLY), with no page file there.
    DISMOUNT refuses it.  If it can't be used, %MOUNT-W-NOSYSVOL says why
    and govax starts from its built-in files, as it does with the option
    --system-file none.  --system-initialize makes the volume again from
    govax's own files, keeping the old container as FILE.old.  See HELP
    CONFIG KEYS for the settings.
